WEBVTT

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.530
<b>Step 11
"DIY" Means Do It Yourself!</b>

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.240
Purin, why don't you do this with us, too?

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.840
With you?

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.950
Building the secret hideout!

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.230
Wh-Why would I do something like that?

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:56.920
It's fun, you know? DIY!

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.860
But I'm not interested 
in that kind of thing.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:03.640
Pudding, you were really good at 
making those accessories, right?

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:04.430
What?

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.520
Accessories?

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.000
Do you mean the ones we made to earn money?

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:16.790
She also helped me create the 
blueprints for the secret hideout.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:20.050
And the person who came up with the idea 
of a tree house in the first place was...

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.630
Shut up!

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.120
Good job, Pudding.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:28.750
Is that how it was?

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.780
Suridecchi, you're pretty good!

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.010
Shut up—

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.130
Thank you.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.730
Let's build it together.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.450
Let's do it!

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.860
Come on, Purin!

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:47.950
Um...

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:52.110
The DIY club aprons...

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:56.650
I wanted to be ready for when 
we had more members, so...

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.590
That's just like you, Takumin!

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.610
P-Please take it.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.410
Go on, Suridecchi!

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.040
Be honest.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.450
Purin!

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.410
Thank you!

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.420
It looks great on you!

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.730
What are you applauding for?

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.820
Honestly, Serufu.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.300
Hold this and turn your back to me.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.610
At least tie this properly.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.660
You are hopeless.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:57.990
And with that decided...

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.920
Purin

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:04.160
"Purin"?

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.120
I-I accidentally wrote my nickname.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.530
I'll rewrite it!

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.920
What's wrong with it? 
It's easy to understand this way.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.930
And Jobko's says "Jobko."

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.050
What's your birth name?

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:16.690
Miku! It's Suride Miku!

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:20.700
Why is Suridecchi's nickname "Purin" anyway?

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:23.440
D-Does it matter?

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.200
Purin, let me see that!

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:25.930
Yasaku Rei

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.640
Yua Serufu

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.430
Hikage Takumi

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.850
Jobko

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.700
Kouki Kokoro

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.700
Purin

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.010
Now we have six members.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:40.970
Though, two of them are 
students from a different school.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:45.440
Well, it's true that they don't 
officially count, but...

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.730
Welcome to the DIY club!

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.930
Welcome!

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.610
I'm looking forward to 
learning from all of you!

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.630
See you later!

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.750
Tomorrow, we start building 
our secret hideout!

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.950
I-It gets your heart racing, doesn't it?

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:22.000
It seems like it's gonna 
be hot again tomorrow.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:40.010
Thanks for inviting me.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:41.500
Huh?

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:44.530
Did you say something?

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.810
Nothing!

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:50.270
I'm going home.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.090
Wait for me!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.080
I have to go get my bag.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:59.290
And all the school buses 
left a long time ago!

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.550
I'll let you ride on the back of my bike!

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:03.240
Two people riding one bike isn't allowed.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.910
Then I guess you'll just 
have to run behind me.

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:07.310
I'd hate that!

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.690
This curry ramen is delicious!

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:17.660
There's rice along the bottom of the bowl.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:23.240
So it will turn into curry rice 
all on its own! It's like magic!

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:29.520
Tomorrow, you'll start building 
your secret hideout.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.660
Be careful not to injure 
yourself, all right?

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:33.570
I know!

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:37.060
I bit my tongue.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:39.520
And after I just told you...

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:52.270
Mom.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:55.320
I finally get to build a tree house.

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:22.600
This is a TAB.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.720
A tree attachment bolt.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.200
This is?

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.060
It's also known as a Garnier limb.

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:30.260
Oh, it's called Garnier-san?

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.470
It's not really called 
"Garnier-san," though.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.790
The fruits of your money-earning labors...

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.330
That's what they are, right?

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.160
Yes.

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:42.260
So, Leadercchi... What role 
does this Garniercchi play?

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:43.150
This will...

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.470
It supports the tree and the tree house.

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:50.170
You drive it into the tree 
trunk and secure it firmly.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.980
It supports the beams.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:53.580
Beams?

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.010
This has taken a sudden turn into sci-fi.

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:02.750
Not like that.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:06.010
Let's see, in Japanese it would be...

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:06.910
Hari.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:09.200
Joist

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:09.200
Hari

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:09.200
Beam!!

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:08.820
Yes, exactly.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.090
<b>Drill a hole into the tree</b>

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.090
<b>Drive it in!!</b>

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.090
4 spots

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:11.000
Drive in the TABs...

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.470
Place on top!!

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:12.840
and they'll support the beams.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.500
Those beams will serve as the 
foundation for the tree house.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.720
BEAM!!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.720
Joist

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.720
Hari

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.720
Joist

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.720
Hari

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.350
<b>Foundation</b>

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:17.640
Tree House

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:17.640
Complete!!

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:20.300
It's an incredibly important 
component, isn't it?

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:21.460
But...

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:24.010
How will you drive those in?

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:25.370
Well...

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:31.890
Waku Waku Wan Wan's truck?

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:35.280
Leadercchi's Papacchi and Mamacchi?

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:41.780
It'd be hard for us to drive in
 the TABs on our own,

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:44.090
so I decided to ask some pros for help.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:47.290
Waku Wan's managing director 
and company president.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:49.420
So, it's finally time to 
start construction, is it?

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:50.350
Yes!

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:52.970
Th-Thank you for your expertise!

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:55.690
This is the first time you're meeting 
our company president, right?

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:59.280
Thank you for always looking after Rei.

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:02.350
Now, let's get started!

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.110
Okay!

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:06.220
How do you use those?

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:07.630
These are for...

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.230
A little higher!

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.170
Around here?

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:23.170
A little more to the right!

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:25.340
Okay!

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.660
That'll do it for that one.

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:47.400
Shii-chan!

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.200
Meow!

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:54.970
What's that?

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:56.760
It's an antiseptic.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:01.780
It helps prevent germs and mold from getting
 inside the hole and causing the wood to rot.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:02.870
I see.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.780
Perfect!

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:08.730
Shii-chan seems to be quite adept at this.

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.020
She could become a truly great climber.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:14.450
Okay! Next, it's my turn.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:24.150
That should do it.

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:25.510
Next comes...

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:45.330
<b>Samurai</b>

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:45.320
It's not quite level.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.690
Lower that side a little.

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:48.510
Will do!

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:53.810
Stop.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:57.950
<b>Samurai</b>

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:57.360
Okay!

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:00.550
Shii-chan, we're taking 
it down for the moment.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:01.470
Okay, meow!

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:10.220
We have to make very sure that 
it's level at this point.

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:13.260
Otherwise, the floor will be slanted.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.160
Company president! 
Managing director!

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.480
Thank you!

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:25.200
Professional work is truly impressive.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:26.690
Good job!

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:32.920
A task like this is no problem at all!

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:36.250
We'll probably ask you to help machine 
lumber and things later, but...

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.300
Sure. Leave it to us!

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:43.010
Then, this is as much as we'll do today.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:44.760
Tomorrow, we start the floor!

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:45.930
Okay!

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:45.930
Meow!

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.270
It's finally started!

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:57.230
We're building our secret hideout!

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:17.690
We need seventeen 
3,000-millimeter boards for the floor.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:20.560
3,000 millimeters...

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:23.460
Exactly three meters.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:40.680
Here, Serufu.

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:41.460
Okay.

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:42.980
Here!

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:44.400
Got it, meow!

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:56.420
I'm home!

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:17.330
You did well today.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.950
Want to stop by Kanegi Fruits?

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:26.380
Then after that, let's head over to TREE.

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:28.510
The classic course, huh?

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:43.910
I-It's very sturdy, isn't it?

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:46.790
That's thanks to our gracious 
and venerable TABs.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.290
Next, we'll set up the frame.

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:51.930
After that, we'll put up the walls and roof.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:54.170
We still have lots to do!

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:55.620
Everyone!

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:58.950
How about a short break?

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.060
Please come down and have some treats!

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.850
Haruko-sensei, thank you so much!

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:12.560
Thank you!

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:16.400
Eat well and then give it 
your very best, all right?

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:21.150
Moving around really makes a person hungry.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:28.930
I'm getting better!

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:31.600
Now I'll be able to do 
my best for a little longer!

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:36.610
Delicious!

00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:38.600
The strawberries are so sweet!

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:42.180
Purin! Want half?

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:46.100
Then I'll give you half of my mango one.

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:48.040
Okay! It's a trade!

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.080
Delicious!

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:02.300
Leadercchi, I'd like to eat 
your cookies again sometime.

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:04.560
R-Really?

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:06.920
Then, I'll bake some for next time.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:08.910
Yay, meow!

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:12.820
I didn't get to eat any last time, 
so make sure to bake lots.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:13.980
All right.

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:17.770
Thank you for the food!

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:21.280
Well, now that we've 
recharged, let's do this!

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:22.470
Okay!

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:22.470
Meow!

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.110
Will this work?

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:38.690
Yeah. Thanks.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.040
Could you do four more, please?

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.080
Will do.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.560
Directorcchi's execution 
is so impressive, meow.

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:47.220
Right, Haru-neechan?

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.180
They say, "for mochi, 
go to a mochi shop," right?

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:55.460
That part there...

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:58.600
It'll get caught in the branches, 
so should we cut them back a little?

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.550
We have to make progress in building 
and on furnishing the interior, right?

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:06.140
Would it be better to split into teams 
and work on them at the same time?

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:09.480
Well, let's see...

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:11.240
What if we did this?

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:12.880
Yeah!

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:13.790
Okay.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.320
The Moulin Rouge.

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:20.470
In French, it means "red mill."

00:16:20.470 --> 00:16:23.200
This building in the 
Montmartre district of Paris

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:26.790
really does have a red windmill on its roof.

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:11.410
Where's Jobko-chan?

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:14.400
After her bath, she fell fast asleep.

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:16.320
Well, it is really tiring, right?

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:22.460
It seems like we'll be able 
to finish by summer vacation.

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:23.750
Somehow.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:26.790
I hope some people who want 
to become members show up.

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:29.890
In order for the club to continue,

00:18:29.890 --> 00:18:33.510
you need two more official members, right?

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:35.850
Yeah. I'm sure they'll come.

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:38.260
Once the secret hideout's finished...

00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:44.400
It's a little bit funny.

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:46.190
What is?

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:52.470
I want to finish the secret 
hideout, but... How can I put it?

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:56.410
This feeling of, "If it's never 
finished, that's okay."

00:18:56.410 --> 00:18:59.820
It's a feeling I can't say I don't feel.

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:04.700
And I feel like it's not that I don't 
have the feeling I feel that way. Maybe?

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.630
What are you saying?

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:08.410
Still...

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:13.790
It's not like I don't 
understand how you feel.

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:15.400
Purin!

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:18.120
After all, it's so much fun.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:19.600
Being with everyone...

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:22.790
and building the secret hideout together.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:27.170
But this is no time for idle chitchat!

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:30.550
Oh, honestly! I have to go study!

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:31.830
Oh, Purin!

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:34.380
Good night!

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:36.900
Good night.

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:07.620
There's not enough.

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:09.350
There won't be enough, will there?

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:16.360
Not enough? For what?

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:17.850
The roof.

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:19.300
The roof?

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:22.700
We don't have enough wood 
to put on the roof.

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:26.110
Everything else is fine.

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:27.490
We have enough for the walls.

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:31.080
But the roof...

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:34.620
The roof, huh?

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:35.980
What do we do, meow?

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:37.940
Should we use silvergrass 
to make it a thatched roof?

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:41.600
Silvergrass? Will we be able 
to gather it by the river?

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:44.940
But at this time of year...

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:47.370
This is quite the problem.

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:54.410
You already spent the funds you raised
 on the TABs and other tools.

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:57.030
Let's just gather wood again!

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:17.820
Just make sure it's from spots 
where it won't be noticed.

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:22.270
The floorboards and walls...

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:25.420
We can use planks from the shelves too!

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:29.680
Okay, meow!

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:38.090
With this much, we should be fine!

00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:39.910
I'm nearly sure of it!

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:47.500
Okay.

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:53.720
One last spurt!

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:58.990
As we approach the completion 
of our secret hideout...

00:21:58.990 --> 00:22:00.980
Do it...

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:04.090
yourself!

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Step 12</b>

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>"DIY" Means Friendship, Always and Forever!</b>
